body:
Confirmed on 4.8 dev (master). I found the root cause and I'm preparing a fix.

I can reproduce this on the current `master` branch. The spam comes from `EditorPropertyPath::_can_drop_data_fw()` in `editor/inspector/editor_properties.cpp`:

```cpp
const Dictionary drag_data = p_data;
if (!drag_data.has("type")) {
    return false;
}
const Vector<String> filesPaths = drag_data["files"];   // <-- accessed before the type is checked

```
The "files" key only exists in the drag data when dragging from the FileSystem dock (editor_node.cpp sets both "type" as "files"/"files_and_dirs" and "files" together). When dragging a node from the Scene dock, the drag data has "type": "nodes" and no "files" key at all — so Dictionary::operator[] hits the ERR_FAIL_NULL_V_MSG in dictionary.cpp on every hover probe, hence the repeated "Please report" messages.

The same happens when dragging a resource over the property (drag data type "resource"), so the node case isn't the only trigger.

The fix is to check the drag type first (matching the pattern used elsewhere, e.g. in filesystem_dock.cpp) and guard the "files" key before accessing it. Drop behavior is unchanged — node/resource drags are still rejected, just silently.

I'll open a PR shortly.
